# Copy this to the PROJECT ROOT as mken.env, then fill it in:
#
#     cd ~/projects/miscellaneous-ken
#     cp deploy/mken.env.example mken.env
#     chmod 600 mken.env
#
# It goes beside agent.py, NOT in deploy/ — run.sh sources ./mken.env from the
# project root. It is gitignored on purpose: this is the only file holding
# secrets, which is why only the .example ships.
#
# Format is read by both `set -a; . ./mken.env` and systemd, so:
#   - no "export"
#   - no quotes around values (systemd treats them as part of the value)
#   - no trailing comments on a value line

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YouTube Data API key — needed for autonomous clip discovery.
#
# This is a plain API key, NOT the OAuth client in client_secret.json. It is
# read-only and cannot touch the channel; uploads still go through token.json.
#
# console.cloud.google.com -> same project as your OAuth client
#   -> APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key
#   -> Edit key -> API restrictions -> restrict to "YouTube Data API v3"
#      (leave Application restrictions at None — a home IP changes.)
#
# Without it the agent still runs, but only from the public-domain channels
# listed in config.json: it cannot search for Creative Commons clips and
# cannot verify licences, so it stays on the safe subset rather than guessing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=AIzaSy_REPLACE_ME

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editorial pick + headline writing — choosing which of ~100 candidates is
# worth posting and writing the headline. Set AT LEAST ONE of the three.
#
# config.json -> editorial.providers sets the order they are tried. The first
# with a key wins; one that fails (no credit, rate limit) falls through to the
# next, so a second key is real insurance rather than clutter.
#
# GEMINI  aistudio.google.com/api-keys — has a FREE tier on flash models.
#         Start here. No card needed, no SDK to install.
# ANTHROPIC  console.anthropic.com -> API keys. Paid; credits are separate
#         from any Claude subscription (Plans & Billing).
# OPENAI  platform.openai.com -> API keys. Paid, prepaid credits.
#         Needs the SDK: pip install openai
#
# Delete or leave commented any you do not use.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GEMINI_API_KEY=REPLACE_ME
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Failure alerts. Create a bot with @BotFather on Telegram; it gives you a
# token like 123456789:AAF... The chat id is already in config.json.
# Optional — the agent runs fine without it, you just find out about failures
# by reading logs/agent.log instead of getting a message.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=REPLACE_ME

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reddit — NOT IN USE. discovery.story_subreddits is empty by design: Reddit's
# Responsible Builder Policy forbids sharing or commercialising Reddit data
# without written approval, and Reddit cannot licence you its users' photos in
# any case. The code path exists; leave these blank unless that changes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
# REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# REDDIT_USER_AGENT=macos:miscellaneous-ken:1.0 (by /u/yourname)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Only matters if YouTube starts refusing downloads ("Sign in to
# confirm you're not a bot"). Export cookies.txt from a signed-in browser and
# point at it here. Unlikely from a home connection.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YTDLP_COOKIES=/Users/dankwawadie/projects/miscellaneous-ken/cookies.txt
